what is JDK :
JDK stands for Java Development Kit. It contains JRE, Debugger, Jar, Javadocs everything you need to develop a
java application.

what is JRE :
JRE stands for Java Runtime Environment. It contains JVM and packages such as java.lang, java.utils everything you
 need to write a java code.

what is JVM :
JVM stands for Java Virtual Machine. It contains compiler like JIT, class loader. It the native code which load
the bytecode, validate the bytecode and execute in machine code.

what is JIT :
JIT stand for for Just In Time - JVM contains JIT compiler. Initially JVM complies the bytecode into machine code.
JIT is able to identifies hot spot (frequently called methods) and complies them into optimize machine instructions
for fast speed.
